1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,890
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,890
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:22,570
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,590
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,590
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:37,270
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:37,350
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:44,520
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:44,520
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:51,860
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:51,860
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,660
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,660
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,610
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,770
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:10,750
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:10,750
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,260
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,260
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,760
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,760
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,570
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,570
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:33,940
Hello, I'm not home right now.

37
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,830
Please leave your message after the beep.

38
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,840
My last job...

39
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,580
The red is as if it's for the color of blood.

40
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:48,540
EPISODE 21
NERV IS BORN

41
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:51,130
Abducted?! The Vice Commander?

42
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:53,210
It happened two hours ago.

43
00:01:53,210 --> 00:01:56,380
He was last seen in District 8 on the west side.

44
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:58,260
That's within our compound!

45
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,550
What was your Intelligence Department doing?!

46
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:03,810
There's an insider who leaked information
and instigated this.

47
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:05,850
He was able to get the better of us.

48
00:02:05,850 --> 00:02:08,560
Someone who can pull the wool over
the eyes of Intelligence Division 2?

49
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,230
It can't be!

50
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:13,980
Ryoji Kaji is the man believed to be
the mastermind behind this.

51
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:16,650
And that's why you're here.

52
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:18,950
We appreciate your quick understanding.

53
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:20,910
As a member of the same organization,

54
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,780
it is regrettable that we must suspect
the Chief of Operations,

55
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,590
but this is pan of our job.

56
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,040
Considering the history between me and him,

57
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,080
it seems like the logical step to take.

58
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,750
Thank you for your cooperation.

59
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:33,340
Take her away.

60
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:36,420
It has been a while, Chairman Kiel.

61
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:39,000
This is quite a rude welcome.

62
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,810
I need not apologize to you for the impropriety.

63
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:45,890
This is a necessary procedure in order
to speak with you at leisure.

64
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:47,930
You certainly haven't changed.

65
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:50,480
Does my convenience mean nothing then?

66
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:53,270
The problem being discussed
is an urgent matter.

67
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:54,900
It was unavoidable.

68
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,530
Please understand.

69
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:59,990
So, it's Seele and not the Committee.

70
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:03,320
We have no intention of creating a new god.

71
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:06,890
We would like your cooperation,
Professor Fuyutsuki.

72
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:09,920
Professor Fuyutsuki...

73
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:11,290
Professor! Professor Fuyutsuki!

74
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:12,750
YEAR 1999, KYOTO

75
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:12,750
Professor! Professor Fuyutsuki!

76
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,460
Oh, it's you two.

77
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:19,170
You wanna join us for some beer in Kamogawa?

78
00:03:19,170 --> 00:03:20,380
Again?

79
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:23,970
Ryoko and the others are saying
they'll go if you go.

80
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:27,140
Our professor was also saying you should
show up once in a while.

81
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,110
Sure, all right.

82
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:32,940
It's good to go out and have
a drink every so often.

83
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,020
Yes, Sir.

84
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,650
You excel at your work,

85
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:39,150
but you don't take socializing seriously
and that's not good.

86
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:40,650
I'm sure you're right.

87
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:42,530
By the way, Fuyutsuki,

88
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:47,120
there's a bioengineering student
who submitted an interesting paper.

89
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:50,160
The student's name is Ikari. Do you know her?

90
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:52,510
Ikari? No, I don't.

91
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:56,210
I told her about you and she said
she was interested in meeting you.

92
00:03:56,210 --> 00:03:59,800
She'll probably contact you eventually,
so take care of things, will you?

93
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:02,260
Ikari, was it? All right.

94
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:03,800
Metaphysical Biology Research Room 1 Fuyutsuki

95
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,350
I read your paper.

96
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:09,770
I found a couple of things questionable,
but it was a stimulating paper.

97
00:04:09,770 --> 00:04:11,350
Thank you very much.

98
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:13,810
Yui Ikari, wasn't it?

99
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:14,900
Yes.

100
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,770
What are your plans for the future?

101
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:18,020
Are you going to find work?

102
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:21,030
Or do you intend to join the research lab here?

103
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:23,400
I haven't thought that far ahead yet.

104
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:26,910
And besides, aren't you forgetting a third option?

105
00:04:26,910 --> 00:04:30,080
I'm also considering a domestic life.

106
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,670
Of course, that's only if I can find someone nice.

107
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,250
BACK IN THE YEAR 2015

108
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:37,420
With an S2 engine on board,

109
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:41,380
Evangelion Unit 01 has become
an absolute being!

110
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:45,090
We have no use for an actualized god.

111
00:04:45,090 --> 00:04:47,430
We must not create a god.

112
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:50,860
We cannot allow that man to create a god.

113
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:54,870
Gendo Ikari, is he a man that can be trusted?

114
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:57,980
Gendo Rokubungi? I've heard of him.

115
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,820
BACK IN THE YEAR 1999

116
00:04:58,730 --> 00:05:01,180
No, I've never met him,

117
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:04,190
but there's always some rumor
going around about him.

118
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:04,190
Kyoto Prefecture Police Department

119
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:08,340
What? He asked to be released
into my custody?

120
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:10,080
No, I'll come.

121
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:12,340
When should I come over there?

122
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:16,450
I heard about you from a certain person,

123
00:05:16,450 --> 00:05:19,050
so I wanted to meet you.

124
00:05:19,590 --> 00:05:23,010
You're a rather coarse man,
to get into a drunken brawl.

125
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:25,970
There was no time to talk.
They just picked a fight with me.

126
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:28,260
I'm not very good at being liked,

127
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:30,730
but I am used to being treated coldly.

128
00:05:31,730 --> 00:05:34,450
Well, it's none of my business anyway.

129
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:36,100
Professor Fuyutsuki,

130
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:39,820
you seem to be exactly the person
I expected you to be.

131
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:44,880
Yes, my first impression of him was of distaste.

132
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:49,660
And back then, seasons and autumn
still existed in this country.

133
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:50,990
Are you serious?

134
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:54,750
Yes, I am seeing Mr. Rokubungi.

135
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:58,630
When I heard that, I wasn't able
to hide my surprise.

136
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,710
I never would have thought you would
share your time with him.

137
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:07,430
Oh, but Professor Fuyutsuki,
he's quite a sweet person.

138
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,430
It's just that no one knows it.

139
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:12,550
Maybe it's more blissful not to know.

140
00:06:12,550 --> 00:06:15,680
Did I inconvenience you by
introducing you to him?

141
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:20,400
No, I'll admit that he's an interesting man,
though I can't get to like him.

142
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:26,240
But within our circle, the common opinion
was that he had approached Yui

143
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:29,440
for her talent and for
the organization backing her.

144
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:34,160
Later, I would hear rumors that this
organization was called Seele.

145
00:06:34,370 --> 00:06:35,830
YEAR 2000, ANTARCTICA

146
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:38,000
The Second Impact.

147
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
That tragedy occurred in the final year
of the 20th century.

148
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:48,510
YEAR 2001

149
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:45,800
And the first year of
the 21st century was pure hell.

150
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,420
There is no other word to describe that year.

151
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:49,430
YEAR 2002

152
00:06:52,230 --> 00:06:55,290
To think this was once a continent of ice...

153
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:57,270
There's no trace of it left.

154
00:06:57,270 --> 00:06:59,110
Professor Fuyutsuki...

155
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,730
You?

156
00:07:00,730 --> 00:07:02,530
I'm surprised you survived.

157
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:06,410
I'd heard that you were a member
of the Katsuragi Research Team.

158
00:07:06,410 --> 00:07:09,610
Luckily, I had returned to Japan
the day before the incident,

159
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:11,530
so I was able to escape the tragedy.

160
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:13,000
I see.

161
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,580
Rokubungi, you...

162
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:17,340
Excuse me, I have a different name now.

163
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:21,210
A postcard? Not a business card?

164
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,620
We're Married

165
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,620
Gendo & Yui
Ikari

166
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,620
It has been
a long time.
Are you doing well?

167
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:26,040
Ikari? Gendo Ikari...

168
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:29,510
My wife has been nagging me to get
this to you, Professor Fuyutsuki.

169
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:31,590
She seems to be a fan of yours.

170
00:07:31,590 --> 00:07:32,760
I'm honored.

171
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:37,010
Gendo & Yui
Ikari

172
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:37,010
It has been
a long time.
Are you doing well?

173
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:35,220
How is Yui doing?

174
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:37,380
Isn't she participating in this expedition?

175
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:41,650
Yui wanted to come, but we
have a child now, so...

176
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:51,200
SAFETY FIRST

177
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:46,190
Your organization... Seele, was it?

178
00:07:46,190 --> 00:07:48,070
I've heard nothing but bad things about it.

179
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:51,670
I can't approve of forcibly
pinning down the board of directors.

180
00:07:51,670 --> 00:07:53,990
You're fastidious as ever.

181
00:07:53,990 --> 00:07:57,280
No clean organization can survive
in this day and age anymore.

182
00:07:57,280 --> 00:08:00,250
The official investigation of the Second Impact...

183
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:03,420
If the investigation team consisted
only of Seele people,

184
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:05,730
you would run into all sons of issues later.

185
00:08:05,730 --> 00:08:08,720
We're just a makeshift solution
to avoid that, aren't we?

186
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:11,510
YEAR 2015

187
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:13,800
NERV HEADQUARTERS - ISOLATION FACILITY 4

188
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:16,550
I still don't handle dark places very well.

189
00:08:16,550 --> 00:08:18,610
All the bad memories come flooding back.

190
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:20,520
Who is she?

191
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,020
She's the sole survivor of the original expedition.

192
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:24,020
YEAR 2002

193
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:27,020
SOUTH POLE INVESTIGATION SHIP - ISOLATION FACILITY 2

194
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:26,230
Her name is Misato Katsuragi.

195
00:08:26,230 --> 00:08:28,900
Katsuragi? She's Dr. Katsuragi's daughter?

196
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:32,790
Yes, she hasn't spoken for
almost two years now.

197
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:34,150
That's terrible.

198
00:08:34,150 --> 00:08:36,280
It attests to the hell that she witnessed.

199
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,950
Her physical injuries have healed,

200
00:08:37,950 --> 00:08:40,790
but psychological wounds do not heal so easily.

201
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,500
I suppose so.

202
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:45,710
SAFETY FIRST

203
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,710
We can't conclude our findings
for our investigation lightly either.

204
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:49,040
This giant of light...
This incident is full of mysteries.

205
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:55,880
United Nations Moves Headquarters to Japan
In Five Years, Candidate is New Tokyo-2
Second Impact Caused by a Massive Meteor
Impossible to Predict or Avoid
Probability of Once in Every Several
Hundred Million Years
Official United Nations Statement
At 20-30% of the Speed of Light

206
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,880
Soon after, the United Nations issued an official statement

207
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:55,880
stating that the Second Impact was caused by a massive meteor.

208
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,800
But from where I stood, I could see

209
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:02,140
that the information had been
blatantly massaged.

210
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:07,310
Behind all this was Seele and hints that
a man named Kiel was involved.

211
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:11,430
And it made me want to learn the
dark truth of that incident.

212
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:12,940
YEAR 2003, HAKONE

213
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:15,150
Even if that might eventually lead me to the name of Yui Ikari.

214
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:15,150
UNITED NATIONS ARTIFICIAL EVOLUTION LABORATORY

215
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:16,950
{DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

216
00:09:16,950 --> 00:09:20,000
Why do you hide the existence
of the giant of light?!

217
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:24,290
You guys knew about the
Second Impact, didn't you?

218
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:24,830
That it would happen on that day?

219
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:26,250
That it would happen on that day?

220
00:09:24,910 --> 00:09:27,290
LABORATORY DIRECTOR GENDO IKARI

221
00:09:27,770 --> 00:09:31,920
You said you were lucky enough
to get out the day before.

222
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:35,970
Was it also luck that you took
all your research with you?!

223
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:41,560
I am surprised that this material
escaped destruction.

224
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:44,820
I did a thorough investigation of your assets.

225
00:09:45,230 --> 00:09:47,850
I'm sure raising a child is expensive,

226
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:50,810
but isn't the amount rather large
for you to have privately?

227
00:09:50,810 --> 00:09:52,900
You impress me, Professor Fuyutsuki.

228
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:55,490
Why not transfer to the department
of economics?

229
00:09:55,490 --> 00:09:58,820
I'm going to go public about Seele
and the Dead Sea Scrolls

230
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:01,170
being secretly behind the Second Impact.

231
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:04,160
I have no intention of letting the people
who caused that get away with it!

232
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,450
Feel free.

233
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:08,420
But before you do, there is something
I would like to show you.

234
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,960
We're going down quite a ways.

235
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,500
Does it worry you?

236
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,720
Somewhat.

237
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:18,880
What is this?

238
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,140
A cavern left behind by someone,
who was not us.

239
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:24,930
Though eighty-nine percent of it is buried.

240
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:28,440
An underground cavern that was originally
a neat spherical shape...

241
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:32,820
All the resources mankind has to offer
are being poured into that facility.

242
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,320
Oh, Professor Fuyutsuki.

243
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:43,910
Akagi, you too?

244
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:47,160
Yes, this is the best place to research

245
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:50,050
the fundamental theories for the
bio-computers of the future.

246
00:10:50,050 --> 00:10:51,500
I see.

247
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,590
I intend to name it Magi.

248
00:10:53,590 --> 00:10:56,890
Magi? After the three wise men from the East?

249
00:10:56,890 --> 00:10:59,040
Is this what you wanted to show me?

250
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,890
No, this way, please.

251
00:11:01,890 --> 00:11:04,100
Ritsuko, I'll be right back.

252
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,430
What is this?

253
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:10,020
Is this that giant?!

254
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:13,400
Here at Gehirn, we call that giant Adam.

255
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,940
But this is not it.

256
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:17,120
It is not the original.

257
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,030
Then...

258
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:23,200
Yes, it is an Eva, made from Adam by man.

259
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,450
An Eva?!

260
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:26,830
This is the Adam Revival Project,

261
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:29,200
generally known as Project E,
and this is our mockup,

262
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,130
<i>Eva Unit 00.</i>

263
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:33,290
A Prototype for a god?!

264
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:34,540
Fuyutsuki,

265
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:38,560
work with me to create a new era
in the history of mankind.

266
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:45,100
YEAR 2015

267
00:11:46,190 --> 00:11:48,100
Excuse me, Ma'am?

268
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:51,810
Oh, I'm sorry. Let's hurry up and retest Rei.

269
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:54,580
I haven't seen Miss Katsuragi around today.

270
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:56,070
You're right.

271
00:11:56,570 --> 00:11:57,900
Miss Katsuragi?

272
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,280
Right! Misato Katsuragi! Nice to meet you!

273
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,240
YEAR 2005
NEW TOKYO-2, NAGANO PREFECTURE

274
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:02,280
Mother,

275
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,740
2ND TOKYO UNIVERSITY, SCHOOL GROUNDS

276
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:05,740
I met a girl named Katsuragi the other day.

277
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:08,700
Other people will only look at me from afar,

278
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:12,210
and each time, I am reminded of
the weight your name carries,

279
00:12:12,210 --> 00:12:16,170
but this girl has no reservation
towards me for some reason.

280
00:12:16,930 --> 00:12:20,720
I am told that she is the sole survivor
of that expedition.

281
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,050
She was apparently aphasic for a time,

282
00:12:23,050 --> 00:12:27,050
but now, she chatters away a mile a minute
as if to make up for lost time.

283
00:12:27,810 --> 00:12:32,110
Ritchan, I am still burrowed underground,
the same as always.

284
00:12:32,110 --> 00:12:34,850
I've grown tired of the lunches they provide.

285
00:12:34,850 --> 00:12:38,020
On the surface, they have apparently begun
working on the plans for New Tokyo-S

286
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:40,330
in accordance with the Second
Capital Transfer Project.

287
00:12:40,830 --> 00:12:43,490
Lately, Misato hadn't been showing up
at the university,

288
00:12:43,490 --> 00:12:46,420
and when I finally got her to tell me why,
it was so idiotic.

289
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:50,660
Apparently, she had been sleeping with
her boyfriend at her apartment,

290
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:52,950
for an entire week!

291
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:55,760
I feel like I have seen an unexpected side of her.

292
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:58,210
She introduced him to me today.

293
00:12:58,210 --> 00:12:59,630
He's good-looking,

294
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:02,640
but I just cannot get to like his frivolous attitude.

295
00:13:03,390 --> 00:13:07,010
As I recall, you have never been
good around boys, Ritchan.

296
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:09,430
In the end, being raised only by a woman...

297
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:12,850
No, I'm sorry. I have left you to your
own devices for so long.

298
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:16,650
It's awful of me to act like a mother
only when it's convenient.

299
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,400
A mother...

300
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,400
YEAR 2004

301
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,900
HAKONE - UNDERGROUND LABORATORY 2

302
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:24,690
LCL electrified. Pressure at plus zero point two.

303
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:26,740
No destrudo readings detected in transmissions.

304
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,450
<i>Para-base is stable.</i>

305
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:29,070
What is this child doing here?

306
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:31,370
He's Director Ikari's son.

307
00:13:31,370 --> 00:13:35,530
Ikari, this is not a nursery school.
Today is a crucial day!

308
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:39,130
I'm sorry, Professor Fuyutsuki.
I'm the one who brought him.

309
00:13:39,130 --> 00:13:42,460
Yui, this is your experiment today.

310
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:43,920
That's why.

311
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:47,280
I want to show my child the bright future.

312
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:50,390
Those were Ms. Yui's final words.

313
00:13:50,390 --> 00:13:54,400
The irregular circumstances erased her
from this world.

314
00:13:54,770 --> 00:13:58,040
Exactly as I had wished.

315
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,170
I am such a horrible woman.

316
00:14:01,170 --> 00:14:04,940
Ritchan, Director Ikari changed after that day.

317
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:08,060
Where have you been for the past week?

318
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:10,950
You're allowed to grieve, but you
need to be aware

319
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:13,580
that you are responsible for
more than yourself now.

320
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:14,950
I know.

321
00:14:14,950 --> 00:14:19,160
Fuyutsuki, I am going to recommend
a new project starting today.

322
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,750
I have already proposed it to Chairman Kiel.

323
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:23,550
You're not going to...

324
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:24,670
That's right.

325
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:27,800
The path to godhood that none have
ever succeeded in before.

326
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,800
The Human Instrumentality Project.

327
00:14:29,930 --> 00:14:30,890
YEAR 2008

328
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,930
Mother,

329
00:14:32,930 --> 00:14:35,520
congratulations on the completion of
the fundamental theory of Magi.

330
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,680
This is not exactly a gift to celebrate it with,

331
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:41,190
but my formal admission into Gehirn
has been unofficially approved.

332
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:44,280
I will be working on Project E
starting next month.

333
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,000
Who's there?

334
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,540
Technology Development Department,
Ritsuko Akagi.

335
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:57,170
Here's my ID.

336
00:14:57,170 --> 00:14:59,160
I heard the command center
had been completed,

337
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:02,130
so I came to see it, but this place is a maze.

338
00:15:02,130 --> 00:15:06,210
If you want the command center,
the Director and Dr. Akagi are there.

339
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:10,180
Are you really sure?

340
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:13,220
Yes, I have no regrets concerning my work.

341
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:16,610
Liar! You just can't forget about Ms. Yui, right?

342
00:15:18,110 --> 00:15:20,570
But I don't mind.

343
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,200
YEAR 2010

344
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,610
GEOFRONT ARTIFICIAL CANOPY

345
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,660
LOWER LEVEL 2 DIRECT SUPPORT AREA (FUTURE LOCATION)

346
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:38,170
That's the headquarters for Gehirn.

347
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:41,660
Good morning, Director.

348
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:43,580
Did you bring your child today?

349
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:46,460
Oh, but you have a son, if I'm not mistaken.

350
00:15:46,460 --> 00:15:48,050
This isn't Shinji.

351
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:50,590
I'm taking care of a friend's daughter.

352
00:15:50,590 --> 00:15:52,720
Her name is Rei Ayanami.

353
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,850
Hello, Rei.

354
00:15:55,690 --> 00:15:58,830
This girl reminds me of someone...

355
00:15:58,830 --> 00:16:00,650
Ms. Yui?

356
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:05,100
All files concerning Rei Ayanami
have been erased already?

357
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,940
It's blank.

358
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:07,860
What does this mean?

359
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:10,070
COMPLETED

360
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:14,790
Magi Casper, Magi Balthasar,
and Magi Melchior.

361
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:17,370
The Magi are the three pans
that make up who I am.

362
00:16:17,370 --> 00:16:22,710
The scientist in me, the mother in me,
and the woman in me.

363
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:25,580
And those three elements will be in
constant conflict with one another.

364
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,730
The three pans of you...

365
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:30,670
The only thing left is to power it up, right?

366
00:16:31,890 --> 00:16:34,090
I'm going to go home early today.

367
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:35,550
Misato's coming back.

368
00:16:35,550 --> 00:16:38,850
That's right, I didn't know she
was a member of Gehirn.

369
00:16:38,850 --> 00:16:40,270
I believe she's in Germany?

370
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:42,480
Yes, she's serving in Branch 3.

371
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,850
Then I suppose it's a long-distance relationship.

372
00:16:44,850 --> 00:16:46,270
I heard they broke up.

373
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:49,440
Oh, and they looked so good together too.

374
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,480
You can never tell with a man and a woman,

375
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,110
because it's not logical.

376
00:16:53,110 --> 00:16:56,000
That cool attitude of yours
certainly hasn't changed.

377
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,210
You're going to let your own
happiness slip away.

378
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:02,540
Happiness is even harder to define.

379
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:05,870
Well, it's been a longtime since
I've gone drinking.

380
00:17:05,870 --> 00:17:07,130
Goodnight.

381
00:17:07,130 --> 00:17:08,720
Goodnight.

382
00:17:21,610 --> 00:17:23,850
Did you want something, Rei?

383
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:25,480
I got lost.

384
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:29,570
Oh, really? Then you want to
leave here with me?

385
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,480
That's okay.

386
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,820
But you won't be able to get home
by yourself, right?

387
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:36,540
That's none of your business, you old hag.

388
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:38,660
What?

389
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:42,010
I can go home by myself,
so leave me alone, you old hag.

390
00:17:42,010 --> 00:17:45,290
It's not nice to call someone an old hag.

391
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,460
But you are an old hag, aren't you?

392
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:51,170
I'm going to get mad. You need
a good scolding from Director Ikari.

393
00:17:51,170 --> 00:17:54,010
That's what the Director calls you.

394
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:54,840
That...

395
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:56,420
He says, “That old hag is pushy,”

396
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:59,020
or that he, “doesn't need that old hag anymore.”

397
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:00,640
He says, “That old hag is pushy,”

398
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,010
or that he, “doesn't need that old hag anymore.”

399
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:05,930
He doesn't need that old hag anymore.

400
00:18:05,930 --> 00:18:10,530
It's what the Director calls you.

401
00:18:16,410 --> 00:18:18,200
You're nothing but a...

402
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,780
It doesn't matter if you die,
you can always be replaced.

403
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:22,440
Rei...

404
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,630
The same as me.

405
00:18:32,710 --> 00:18:36,590
The Human Instrumentality Project Committee,
chaired by Kiel Lorenz,

406
00:18:36,590 --> 00:18:39,760
dissolved the research organization,
Gehirn, the next day.

407
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,850
And they formed the special duty
organization, Nerv,

408
00:18:41,850 --> 00:18:44,350
as the organization that would
carry out all projects.

409
00:18:44,350 --> 00:18:48,270
All of us were moved directly into Nerv,

410
00:18:48,270 --> 00:18:53,570
with the exception of one, Dr. Akagi,
the remarkable creator of the Magi System.

411
00:18:53,610 --> 00:18:54,570
YEAR 2015

412
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:00,990
Oh, it's you.

413
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:02,490
Long time no see.

414
00:19:02,490 --> 00:19:05,600
I've put the guards outside to sleep for a while.

415
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,960
This will cost you your life.

416
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,330
I just want to get closer to the truth

417
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:13,220
within myself.

418
00:19:15,210 --> 00:19:17,930
Thank you very much for your cooperation.

419
00:19:18,890 --> 00:19:20,380
Is it over?

420
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:23,350
Yes, the problem has been resolved, so...

421
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,310
I see.

422
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,600
What about him?

423
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,190
I do not know.

424
00:19:42,710 --> 00:19:45,500
Hey, you're late.

425
00:19:50,210 --> 00:19:51,840
I'm home.

426
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,810
Play

427
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,810
Messages

428
00:20:25,870 --> 00:20:29,290
Play

429
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:35,440
Katsuragi, it's me.

430
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:37,880
I've probably put you through a lot of trouble

431
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:40,820
by the time you're listening to this.

432
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,470
I'm sorry.

433
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:45,140
Tell Ritchan I said I'm sorry too.

434
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:47,640
Also, since I've troubled you so much anyway,

435
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:50,060
there's this flower I've been growing...

436
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:52,860
It'd make me happy if you'd water it for me.

437
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,780
Shinji knows where it is.

438
00:20:56,320 --> 00:21:00,120
Katsuragi, the truth is with you.

439
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,660
Go forward without any hesitation.

440
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:06,540
If I ever get to see you again,

441
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:09,680
I'll say the words I wasn't able
to say eight years ago.

442
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,540
Bye.

443
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:14,460
Message recorded at 12:02pm.

444
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,790
Jerk...

445
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:23,010
You're really such a jerk...

446
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:49,620
Right then, all I could do was
run away from Misato.

447
00:21:50,210 --> 00:21:54,710
There was nothing I could do or say.
I was a child.

448
00:21:56,090 --> 00:21:57,420
It made me realize that.

449
00:21:57,460 --> 00:22:00,630
TO BE CONTINUED

450
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:06,940
PREVIEW

451
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:10,360
Asuka falls into a psychological pitfall
due to having lost to Shinji.

452
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:12,740
Furthermore, the psychological attack
from an Angel

453
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:14,780
delivers the finishing blow to Asuka's mind.

454
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:18,000
Shinji is unable to offer her
any words of comfort.

455
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,540
Next time, "At Least, Be Human"

456
00:23:18,370 --> 00:23:21,080
AT LEAST, BE HUMAN
